# GRADUATED (R48) from a both-lanes known gap. `.map()` with an INLINE CLOSURE
# that changes the element type used to mint its accumulator from the INPUT
# element type, so a `String` result came back as a raw pointer at rc 0.
#
#     Vector[int] nums = [3, 4]
#     auto v = nums.map((int n): mk("t", "ag"))
#     print(v.get(0).unwrap())    # printed e.g. 187651356173072, not "tag"
#
# ⚠ THE COMPREHENSION EQUIVALENT WAS CORRECT ALL ALONG:
#
#     auto v = [mk("t", "ag") for n in nums]
#
# and that was the whole point: the same mint class, fixed once at the
# comprehension producer, surviving at a SIBLING producer. Both producers now
# read the same channel — `try_lower_vector_hof`'s map/filter arm goes through
# `comp_reserve`/`comp_note_elem`/`comp_close`, so the accumulator is minted
# from the MATERIALIZED element rather than from the receiver's.
#
# ⚠ The old self-host discriminator was the CALLEE SHAPE — an earlier round
# gated cross-type `map` on `fn_sigs` return types for NAMED callees only, so
# `map(label)` was right and the identical `map((int n): …)` was wrong. The old
# RUST-lane discriminator was the DESTINATION: `auto` was wrong and
# `Vector[String]` was right, for both callee shapes.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 2 then tag.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Vector[int] nums = [3, 4]
    auto v = nums.map((int n): mk("t", "ag"))
    print(v.len())
    print(v.get(0).unwrap())
